---@field metadata? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field error? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.
---@field name? string The server-assigned name, which is only unique within the same service that originally returns it. If you use the default HTTP mapping, the `name` should be a resource name ending with `operations/{unique_id}`.
---@field response? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.
---@field done? boolean If the value is `false`, it means the operation is still in progress. If `true`, the operation is completed, and either `error` or `response` is available.

---@alias gcp.servicenetworking_v1.OperationList gcp.servicenetworking_v1.Operation[]

---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PatchServicesConnectionsRequest
---@field service? string Output only. The name of the peering service that's associated with this connection, in the following format: `services/{service name}`.
---@field network? string Required. The name of service consumer's VPC network that's connected with service producer network, in the following format: `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`. `{project}` is a project number, such as in `12345` that includes the VPC service consumer's VPC network. `{network}` is the name of the service consumer's VPC network.
---@field reservedPeeringRanges? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.StringList The name of one or more allocated IP address ranges for this service producer of type `PEERING`. Note that invoking CreateConnection method with a different range when connection is already established will not modify already provisioned service producer subnetworks. If CreateConnection method is invoked repeatedly to reconnect when peering connection had been disconnected on the consumer side, leaving this field empty will restore previously allocated IP ranges.
---@field peering? string Output only. The name of the VPC Network Peering connection that was created by the service producer.
---@field force? boolean If a previously defined allocated range is removed, force flag must be set to true.
---@field name string Required. The private service connection that connects to a service producer organization. The name includes both the private service name and the VPC network peering name in the format of `services/{peering_service_name}/connections/{vpc_peering_name}`. For Google services that support this functionality, this is `services/servicenetworking.googleapis.com/connections/servicenetworking-googleapis-com`.
---@field updateMask? string The update mask. If this is omitted, it defaults to "*". You can only update the listed peering ranges.

---DNS domain suffix for which requests originating in the producer VPC network are resolved in the associated consumer VPC network.
---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PeeredDnsDomain
---@field name? string Required. User assigned name for this resource. Must be unique within the consumer network. The name must be 1-63 characters long, must begin with a letter, end with a letter or digit, and only contain lowercase letters, digits or dashes.
---@field dnsSuffix? string The DNS domain name suffix e.g. `example.com.`. Cloud DNS requires that a DNS suffix ends with a trailing dot.

---@alias gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PeeredDnsDomainList gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PeeredDnsDomain[]

---Grouping of IAM role and IAM member.
---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PolicyBinding
---@field role? string Required. Role to apply. Only allowlisted roles can be used at the specified granularity. The role must be one of the following: - 'roles/container.hostServiceAgentUser' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/compute.securityAdmin' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/compute.networkAdmin' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/tpu.xpnAgent' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/dns.admin' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/logging.admin' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/monitoring.viewer' applied on the shared VPC host project - 'roles/servicemanagement.quotaViewer' applied on the shared VPC host project
---@field member? string Required. Member to bind the role with. See /iam/docs/reference/rest/v1/Policy#Binding for how to format each member. Eg. - user:myuser@mydomain.com - serviceAccount:my-service-account@app.gserviceaccount.com

---@alias gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PolicyBindingList gcp.servicenetworking_v1.PolicyBinding[]

---Represents a range reservation.
---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.RangeReservation
---@field requestedRanges? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.StringList Optional. The name of one or more allocated IP address ranges associated with this private service access connection. If no range names are provided all ranges associated with this connection will be considered. If a CIDR range with the specified IP prefix length is not available within these ranges the validation fails.
---@field secondaryRangeIpPrefixLengths? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.IntegerList Optional. The size of the desired secondary ranges for the subnet. Use usual CIDR range notation. For example, '29' to find unused x.x.x.x/29 CIDR range. The goal is to determine that the allocated ranges have enough free space for all the requested secondary ranges. GCE disallows subnets with prefix_length > 29
---@field ipPrefixLength? number Required. The size of the desired subnet. Use usual CIDR range notation. For example, '29' to find unused x.x.x.x/29 CIDR range. The goal is to determine if one of the allocated ranges has enough free space for a subnet of the requested size. GCE disallows subnets with prefix_length > 29
---@field subnetworkCandidates? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SubnetworkList Optional. List of subnetwork candidates to validate. The required input fields are `name`, `network`, and `region`. Subnetworks from this list which exist will be returned in the response with the `ip_cidr_range`, `secondary_ip_cider_ranges`, and `outside_allocation` fields set.

---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.RemoveServicesDnsRecordSetsRequest
---@field dnsRecordSet? gcp.servicenetworking_v1.DnsRecordSet Required. The DNS record set to remove.
---@field zone? string Required. The name of the private DNS zone in the shared producer host project from which the record set will be removed.
---@field consumerNetwork? string Required. The network that the consumer is using to connect with services. Must be in the form of projects/{project}/global/networks/{network} {project} is the project number, as in '12345' {network} is the network name.
---@field parent string Required. The service that is managing peering connectivity for a service producer's organization. For Google services that support this functionality, this value is `services/servicenetworking.googleapis.com`.

---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.RemoveServicesDnsZonesRequest
---@field consumerNetwork? string Required. The network that the consumer is using to connect with services. Must be in the form of projects/{project}/global/networks/{network} {project} is the project number, as in '12345' {network} is the network name.
---@field name? string Required. The name for both the private zone in the shared producer host project and the peering zone in the consumer project.
---@field parent string Required. The service that is managing peering connectivity for a service producer's organization. For Google services that support this functionality, this value is `services/servicenetworking.googleapis.com`.

---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SearchRangeServicesRequest
---@field network? string Required. Network name in the consumer project. This network must have been already peered with a shared VPC network using CreateConnection method. Must be in a form 'projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}'. {project} is a project number, as in '12345' {network} is network name.
---@field ipPrefixLength? number Required. The prefix length of the IP range. Use usual CIDR range notation. For example, '30' to find unused x.x.x.x/30 CIDR range. Actual range will be determined using allocated range for the consumer peered network and returned in the result.
---@field parent string Required. This is in a form services/{service}. {service} the name of the private access management service, for example 'service-peering.example.com'.

---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SecondaryIpRange
---@field rangeName? string Name of the secondary IP range.
---@field ipCidrRange? string Secondary IP CIDR range in `x.x.x.x/y` format.

---@alias gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SecondaryIpRangeList gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SecondaryIpRange[]

---@class gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SecondaryIpRangeSpec
---@field rangeName? string Required. A name for the secondary IP range. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply with RFC1035. The name must be unique within the subnetwork.
---@field requestedAddress? string Optional. The starting address of a range. The address must be a valid IPv4 address in the x.x.x.x format. This value combined with the IP prefix range is the CIDR range for the secondary IP range. The range must be within the allocated range that is assigned to the private connection. If the CIDR range isn't available, the call fails.
---@field ipPrefixLength? number Required. The prefix length of the secondary IP range. Use CIDR range notation, such as `30` to provision a secondary IP range with an `x.x.x.x/30` CIDR range. The IP address range is drawn from a pool of available ranges in the service consumer's allocated range.
---@field outsideAllocationPublicIpRange? string Optional. Enable outside allocation using public IP addresses. Any public IP range may be specified. If this field is provided, we will not use customer reserved ranges for this secondary IP range.

---@alias gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SecondaryIpRangeSpecList gcp.servicenetworking_v1.SecondaryIpRangeSpec[]

